                <pb facs="0297" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg239"/>


                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>We have received files of the Diario del Imperio to the 18th of May.</p>
                <p>The following decree concerning the establishment of newspapers has been issued
                    by Maximilian:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Article</hi> 1. For the establishment of any
                    newspaper or publication which is to start at a fixed time or otherwise, and is
                    to be engaged in public affairs, the permission of the authorities will be
                    required—this being only granted by our government, and, as our delegates, by
                    the imperial commission or the prefect.</p>
                <p>“Our minister of government is charged with the execution of the present
                    decree.</p>
                <p>“Given in the city of Mexico, the 6th day of May, 1866.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>“MAXIMILIAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>“For the emperor:</p>
                    <p>“The Minister of Government, <hi rendition="#small-caps">“José Salazar
                            Ilarregui.”</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
